Experiment1: one-byte ramdisk but empty header command line.
fastboot -s 00001EB100006FAB flash boot boot.img
Read back full BOOT via oem cat:/dev/mmcblk0p7 + get_staged, verified candidate
prefix byte-for-byte before issuing fastboot reboot. Target returned in 5.7s
on USB devnum22, with ADB shell working and possible=online=0.
Stock aboot injected mem=100M console=null. DT still contained the correct
six firmware RAM banks, but /proc/iomem was80000000-863fffff; MemTotal94608kB,
CMA0. SMEM reservation/ioremap failed. This is observed hardware behavior,
not speculation based on wrapper format alone.

Experiment2: change ONLY header command line to
  earlycon=msm_serial_dm,0x16440000 console=ttyMSM0,115200n8
Repack, BOOT-only flash, full readback check, cold reboot. Kernel+DTB bytes
remain identical to experiment1. ADB returned; possible=online=0;
/proc/iomem restored all firmware banks starting80200000; MemTotal925332kB;
CmaTotal65536kB; active console ttyMSM0; SMEM warnings disappeared.
Kernel code resource is still absent from this RAM map, consistent with a
separate appended-DTB decompressor base issue. That is not claimed fixed by
this header change and is under separate investigation. No kexec attempted.

